# Day 23

**26km / 11 hours**

Yes 11 hours. This was a long and taxing day. It started well enough with a gentle road walk followed by some uphill section on farmland, however the rain had set in by this point and the visibility was atrocious with the clouds around. 

![Most of my early trek was just this, not the best view](./cloudy.jpg)

After this and skirting around for a while I finally entered the forest which promised some kind of respite from the rain but didn't really deliver. The ground was very muddy at this point in many places, accentuated by the rain falling on and off. This is the main reason for this day taking so long: when going down or up through the mud it's very tricky to keep your footing steady so I was taking extra caution to stay upright. 

After a while of this I came to the road around noon and was hoping for a nice shelter to rest up, eat some lunch and escape from the rain which was threatening to get worse. However there was disappointingly no shelter to be found so I continued onward as the rain became extremely heavy and the temperature dropped significantly. So I was cold and wet and still walking. Eventually I came to the entrance for the next section of the walk and continued onward.

This was the worst part of the day as I was cold and miserable and hadn't had a proper break since there wasn't a good place to stop. Still I marched onward. 

Finally after some hours and crossing a stream twice, the sun broke through as the rain died down. Hallelujah! Also I had made progress and made it to the campsite so I sat down, had a bite for a very late lunch and dried a little. Still it seemed a little early to stop (about 3pm) and the campsite was pretty rudimentary, not having a shelter. I made the decision to push on to the next campsite. 

![Leaving the valley behind with the beautiful sun shining](./valley.jpg)

I pushed on with a spring in my step, the track mostly pretty easy at this point only to come to more of the same issue with muddy ups and downs slowing progress significantly. With the sunlight hours running out, I got to the final kilometre which was much easier and easy to walk with stairs before getting to the campsite with a bit of sunlight remaining. 

This was a really difficult day and I'll have to plan ahead more if there are to be more days like it but it was enjoyable eventually.